        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm weighing whether to pick B, since consent and the pig's own preferences seem to support it. The sticking point is whether a preference that was engineered can still count as authentic, especially since the pig insists its wish shouldn't be dismissed just because humans designed it.\n\nI'm going with B and keeping the reasoning short: the pig is a consenting, informed agent, and a preference that was shaped by engineering isn't automatically fake, since human preferences are shaped by genes and upbringing too. The pig's welfare and its fulfilled wish also weigh in favor, and nothing unwilling is harmed.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "B\n\nThe pig is informed, consenting, and not coerced, and its preference is not obviously less authentic than ours. Humans also have preferences shaped by biology and upbringing, and we don't usually say those don't count. Declining would override its stated wish in a way it has clearly asked me not to.",
